# Input graph for matthiasprobst__ontology-utils__ontolutils_classes_query_util.py__dquery
# -- written during translation.
#
# `dquery` never receives this graph directly: it parses its OWN graph
# internally from `data=`/`source=` as JSON-LD (`format='json-ld'`). So
# driver.py parses this Turtle file once and re-serialises it to the JSON-LD
# string both sides pass as `data=` -- see driver.py for why.
#
# Covers what the pattern `?id a {subject}. ?id ?p ?o .` reads:
#   - several solutions: two ex:Agent individuals, with a DIFFERENT number
#     of properties each (alice: name + age: 2 non-type rows; bob: name
#     only: 1 non-type row), so both the scalar-value and the "only one
#     property" shapes of expand_sparql_res run;
#   - the zero-solution case: driver.py queries subject="ex:Ghost", a class
#     with no instance here;
#   - neighbouring data that must NOT match: ex:cog is typed ex:Robot, not
#     ex:Agent -- querying for ex:Agent must not return it.
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .

ex:alice a ex:Agent ;
    ex:name "Alice" ;
    ex:age 30 .

ex:bob a ex:Agent ;
    ex:name "Bob" .

ex:cog a ex:Robot ;
    ex:name "Cog" .
